                                        "sense_id": "a8bc18d7-78a5-32d3-bbe0-f1f1ef66bc8f",
                                        "entry_id": "c770469b-eb51-32f6-81cc-73459a2119a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A graphical representation of a chronological sequence of events (past or future)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "482ddc40-4309-4775-a203-089e4851d817",
                                                "sense_id": "a8bc18d7-78a5-32d3-bbe0-f1f1ef66bc8f",
                                                "text": "I got bitches askin' me about the code for the Wi-Fi / So they can talk about they timeline / And show me pictures of they friends"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46d53d58-8708-43e8-8813-bdd94490927e",
                                                "sense_id": "a8bc18d7-78a5-32d3-bbe0-f1f1ef66bc8f",
                                                "text": "But, as things stand, there's no timeline in place for reopening."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09c024e9-bb40-390b-8f6c-09d7f01909c0",
                                        "entry_id": "c770469b-eb51-32f6-81cc-73459a2119a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A schedule of activities; a timetable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e684628f-da74-3caa-a934-0bc58563214f",
                                        "entry_id": "c770469b-eb51-32f6-81cc-73459a2119a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An individual universe or reality, especially a parallel/alternate one in which events differ from actual history, or differ from the established canon of a fictional world."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44b9235a-5433-4c3f-8b00-18b2be391475",
                                                "sense_id": "e684628f-da74-3caa-a934-0bc58563214f",
                                                "text": "on an alternate timeline"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b1eee33-a12e-4359-a500-ef2ce4c6d2ee",
                                                "sense_id": "e684628f-da74-3caa-a934-0bc58563214f",
                                                "text": "SISKO: I don't quite know how to say this... but now that we know about the accident that sent the ship back in time, we should be able to avoid it.\nWORF: Well if we do that, your timeline will collapse and everything here will cease to exist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad4fb955-b829-447b-9d51-1df9a2591ebe",
                                                "sense_id": "e684628f-da74-3caa-a934-0bc58563214f",
                                                "text": "So in that sense, if we want to talk about the timeline of what it would mean for Trump to be winning and reshifting the Constitutional order, part of what I think about is: If the neoliberal order is cracked, as Gerstle says it is, then the question is: What will succeed it?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
